WEBVTT

00:00.650 --> 00:02.950
The Pokémon Elections 720!

00:03.860 --> 00:07.000
These Pokémon Elections will determine the Pokémon that will be given away during the movie!

00:08.070 --> 00:11.510
We will now start taking your votes via the data broadcast!

00:12.790 --> 00:16.260
Push the d-button on your remote control and vote for the Pokémon you want!

00:16.860 --> 00:18.650
All right, the anime starts now!

00:22.000 --> 00:31.880
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:24.200 --> 00:25.340
A crisis in Kalos...?

00:26.360 --> 00:27.870
I don't know exactly...

00:28.640 --> 00:30.710
...what kind of disaster it is;

00:31.420 --> 00:33.920
I just thought I should let you know.

00:35.200 --> 00:35.620
However...

00:36.600 --> 00:41.520
...the green flames will pull in everything, including both humans and Pokémon.

00:42.760 --> 00:45.990
And Satoshi-kun and his friends are involved in this crisis...

00:46.870 --> 00:49.120
Please tell me one last thing.

00:50.460 --> 00:51.820
What are those "deep green eyes" referring to?

00:52.150 --> 00:53.490
What I saw was...

00:53.850 --> 00:54.320
...this!

01:01.350 --> 01:01.820
Could this be...

01:02.760 --> 01:03.040
...Zygarde?

01:13.300 --> 01:19.010
Satoshi VS Champion Carne!
VS Mega Sirknight!!

01:19.980 --> 01:29.800
As Satoshi continues his journey towards the Eisetsu Gym to obtain the eighth badge, he keeps training so that he can control Gekkouga's mysterious power.

01:30.700 --> 01:31.570
Ready?

01:32.080 --> 01:32.710
Start!

01:36.610 --> 01:39.000
At this speed it'll be a bit of a challenge to dodge them.

01:49.250 --> 01:51.010
I see, so that's how you evade them.

01:51.400 --> 01:52.670
All right!

01:55.500 --> 01:56.470
I won't fall behind!

02:05.090 --> 02:05.530
Me too!

02:14.180 --> 02:15.870
Ow...

02:18.800 --> 02:19.570
Ah, no.

02:20.070 --> 02:23.180
I need to do this much, otherwise we won't be able to use that power.

02:24.780 --> 02:26.060
Let's continue, Gekkouga!

02:32.770 --> 02:34.670
Satoshi and Gekkouga are late.

02:36.380 --> 02:40.320
"I'll become a Pokémon!"... Who <i>thinks</i> like that?

02:42.300 --> 02:45.230
Training is nice and all, but I don't want him to do anything reckless.

02:46.330 --> 02:47.350
Oh, here they are!

02:54.080 --> 02:55.750
Gekkouga's reached the goal!

02:56.290 --> 02:57.730
Satoshi, do your best!

02:57.950 --> 02:59.170
You're almost there!

03:00.720 --> 03:02.240
Satoshi's reached the goal!

03:08.500 --> 03:10.320
Gekkouga, you're too fast...

03:12.210 --> 03:13.350
Satoshi, here.

03:13.750 --> 03:15.070
Oh, thank you.

03:16.040 --> 03:18.880
So did you get closer to Gekkouga?

03:19.590 --> 03:20.030
Yeah.

03:20.450 --> 03:23.030
It's only little by little, but I do get the feeling I'm growing closer to it.

03:24.760 --> 03:25.210
What?

03:27.630 --> 03:29.350
So there is no doubt that's them, right?

03:29.910 --> 03:30.210
None.

03:30.780 --> 03:32.210
I'm going to descend, then.

03:32.480 --> 03:35.700
Carne-san, please remember that you'll be doing a commercial after this,

03:36.070 --> 03:37.700
so please no dangerous...

03:38.610 --> 03:40.240
You don't need to go lower than this.

03:40.650 --> 03:41.910
Please come pick me up later.

03:41.910 --> 03:43.780
Hey, Carne-san!

03:46.370 --> 03:47.380
Are you all right?

03:48.040 --> 03:49.250
No problem.

03:51.040 --> 03:51.790
It's been a while.

03:52.570 --> 03:53.500
Carne-san!

03:54.110 --> 03:57.590
Again, please make sure not to do anything dangerous!

03:58.540 --> 04:00.140
Carne-san, what are you doing here?

04:00.790 --> 04:02.150
Did something happen?

04:02.550 --> 04:05.220
"Did something happen?" I came to see <i>you!</i>

04:06.140 --> 04:07.680
I heard Gojika-san's prediction.

04:09.810 --> 04:11.690
Who would've thought following the brats...

04:12.230 --> 04:18.310
...would lead us to Carne, Champion of Kalos and a movie superstar.

04:22.320 --> 04:23.290
Her beauty,

04:24.070 --> 04:24.950
popularity...

04:25.420 --> 04:27.340
...and her prowess as an actress...

04:28.010 --> 04:31.250
...are all minimal compared to mine.

04:31.760 --> 04:33.830
I guess she can't even be considered a rival.

04:35.930 --> 04:36.950
You got a problem?!

04:39.480 --> 04:41.340
Do you mean this "Kalos crisis"?

04:42.050 --> 04:44.980
Yes. That's why I've done some research.

04:46.300 --> 04:46.700
Look.

04:47.280 --> 04:48.360
What is this?

04:49.110 --> 04:51.800
This island used to be thriving with nature.

04:52.170 --> 04:53.620
Huh? Really?

04:54.390 --> 04:55.720
It's not just this island.

04:56.200 --> 04:58.800
There are already many abnormal incidents happening all over Kalos.

04:59.340 --> 05:00.150
Just what happened there?

05:00.880 --> 05:02.720
We don't know anything for sure yet.

05:03.450 --> 05:06.620
But if these abnormal incidents are the crisis the prediction was referring to,

05:06.980 --> 05:09.580
it's possible that Zygarde has already started taking action as well.

05:10.100 --> 05:10.700
"Zygarde"?

05:11.960 --> 05:12.590
It's a Pokémon.

05:15.750 --> 05:17.090
Could that be...

05:21.430 --> 05:24.270
...the one the lame glasses guys were after?

05:24.510 --> 05:25.260
Hm...

05:25.930 --> 05:27.390
Zygarde is the Order Pokémon.

05:28.390 --> 05:29.870
It lives deep inside a cave,

05:30.390 --> 05:33.840
and, when a crisis befalls the Kalos region,

05:34.510 --> 05:35.910
is said to reveal itself...

05:36.690 --> 05:37.730
...and protect the land of Kalos.

05:38.420 --> 05:40.120
"Protect the land of Kalos"?

05:40.460 --> 05:41.350
"Zygarde"?

05:42.790 --> 05:44.250
If I recall correctly,

05:45.240 --> 05:47.280
A disaster in the near future.

05:48.490 --> 05:50.780
One which you people are associated with.

05:52.130 --> 05:53.910
we have something to do with this crisis...

05:54.490 --> 05:57.290
That's right. It concerned me a little, so I came to see you.

05:57.890 --> 06:00.530
Satoshi-kun, have there been any strange incidents happening around you and your friends?

06:03.930 --> 06:04.550
That's right!

06:05.050 --> 06:07.220
Satoshi's Gekkouga is amazing!

06:10.700 --> 06:11.740
Is that what happened?

06:12.310 --> 06:14.280
That is something Gojika-san had mentioned as well.

06:15.160 --> 06:16.560
However, this one's future...

06:17.130 --> 06:20.250
...is you two climbing up towards a future of new greatness...

06:21.210 --> 06:24.910
...that no one has ever seen before.

06:26.420 --> 06:27.960
Gekkouga and Satoshi-kun...

06:30.290 --> 06:32.410
Satoshi-kun, will you show it to me?

06:36.930 --> 06:40.000
Let's have a battle with my Sirknight here.

06:40.880 --> 06:43.590
I want to see Gekkouga's power myself.

06:44.360 --> 06:48.140
Okay! Being able to have a Pokémon battle with you is the greatest, Carne-san!

06:48.660 --> 06:49.910
Let's do our best, Gekkouga!

06:52.680 --> 06:54.360
This is our chance.

06:54.360 --> 06:59.280
If we make use of their focus on the battle, we might be able to get ourselves a mega evolving Sirknight.

07:00.290 --> 07:05.600
It's nowhere near worthy as an opponent, but if you're pinning your hopes on me, I guess I have no choice...

07:06.140 --> 07:08.830
Right... Make sure to...

07:08.830 --> 07:10.280
...steal that Sirknight...

07:17.940 --> 07:18.840
What are those?

07:19.100 --> 07:20.380
It's one of Citron's inventions.

07:21.000 --> 07:22.600
They are called "Battle Pulse Measuring Instruments",

07:22.960 --> 07:25.380
and measure Satoshi and Gekkouga's degree of synchronization.

07:26.440 --> 07:31.400
Those measurements are then sent to the Citroid Mini here, which turns them into holograms.

07:34.520 --> 07:40.230
Red and blue waves indicate the changes in Satoshi and Gekkouga in real time.

07:40.800 --> 07:41.310
I see.

07:41.960 --> 07:42.680
Gekkouga,

07:43.060 --> 07:48.420
in our last battle with Carne-san, we got defeated even before Sirknight mega evolved.

07:54.440 --> 07:57.110
But we've gained a lot of experience since then.

07:58.250 --> 07:59.320
Let's win, no matter what!

08:00.690 --> 08:02.170
Carne-san, please bear with us.

08:02.900 --> 08:03.210
Yeah.

08:10.230 --> 08:11.430
All right, come at us!

08:11.990 --> 08:12.680
All right.

08:12.680 --> 08:14.360
Gekkouga, Cut!

08:21.910 --> 08:22.970
They really are amazing.

08:23.330 --> 08:25.340
They can communicate via mere eye contact!

08:27.250 --> 08:27.860
Water Shuriken!

08:32.980 --> 08:34.350
Use Cut repeatedly!

08:41.220 --> 08:42.000
Aerial Ace!

08:49.900 --> 08:50.630
It dodged again...

08:52.090 --> 08:53.520
At this rate, this is going to end up like last time.

08:54.090 --> 08:56.110
Sirknight is too fast; we can't get a hold of it.

09:01.180 --> 09:02.440
I expected nothing less from Carne-san.

09:02.720 --> 09:06.540
Dealing damage to the Champion of Kalos will not be that easy.

09:07.110 --> 09:09.120
Satoshi, do your best!

09:12.280 --> 09:13.750
It's well raised, but...

09:14.240 --> 09:16.660
...I don't sense any difference from other Gekkouga.

09:17.620 --> 09:19.040
Maybe <i>we</i> should try making a move this time.

09:19.750 --> 09:20.410
Shadow Ball!

09:22.890 --> 09:23.380
It moved!

09:24.850 --> 09:25.460
Gekkouga!

09:25.840 --> 09:26.760
Double Team!

09:32.950 --> 09:33.380
All right!

09:33.800 --> 09:34.920
Shoot them all down in one go!

09:35.320 --> 09:36.140
Shadow Ball!

09:46.370 --> 09:47.760
Gekkouga, are you all right?

09:49.210 --> 09:50.070
That's the spirit!

09:50.830 --> 09:52.110
They are no changes in the waves.

09:52.810 --> 09:54.440
Use Water Shuriken repeatedly!

10:04.500 --> 10:05.620
She predicts our every move.

10:08.270 --> 10:09.050
Moonblast!

10:15.730 --> 10:15.970
Dodge!

10:20.330 --> 10:20.890
Gekkouga!

10:24.600 --> 10:25.110
Gekkouga!

10:27.100 --> 10:27.920
Can you continue?

10:33.280 --> 10:34.590
I have an idea.

10:36.520 --> 10:37.080
Gekkouga,

10:37.500 --> 10:38.980
use Water Shuriken on Sirknight!

10:49.190 --> 10:50.880
Go! Cut!

10:53.920 --> 10:54.920
You did it, Gekkouga!

10:59.020 --> 11:00.100
Th-This is...!

11:02.670 --> 11:03.940
They got us.

11:06.130 --> 11:07.690
Much, much stronger!

11:07.990 --> 11:09.310
Let's go!

11:22.690 --> 11:23.820
Wh-What?!

11:23.820 --> 11:27.120
The brat boy and Gekkouga fused!

11:37.690 --> 11:38.870
Pokémon Quiz.

11:39.290 --> 11:40.410
The answer is...?

11:42.580 --> 11:44.740
The Pokémon Elections 720!

11:45.570 --> 11:49.260
Push the d-button on your remote control and vote for the Pokémon you want!

11:50.020 --> 11:59.990
Coming up next:

11:50.020 --> 11:55.020
Sirknight finally mega evolves!

11:50.970 --> 11:55.650
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

11:55.020 --> 11:59.990
What will be the outcome of the battle...!?

12:07.210 --> 12:08.680
Carne-san, this is it!

12:09.490 --> 12:11.440
Please watch our power!

12:12.830 --> 12:15.880
It's true... I've never seen a Gekkouga like this before.

12:16.340 --> 12:17.190
Cut!

12:25.220 --> 12:26.040
Shadow Ball!

12:32.860 --> 12:34.680
Had that hit, we wouldn't have stood a chance.

12:38.550 --> 12:41.570
Satoshi-kun and his friends always surprise us.

12:42.440 --> 12:44.150
But is that Gekkouga...

12:44.590 --> 12:46.030
...in any way related to the prediction?

12:46.640 --> 12:48.050
The answer lies in this battle.

12:49.330 --> 12:50.140
Shadow Ball!

12:52.030 --> 12:52.750
Water Shuriken!

12:59.800 --> 13:00.860
Cut!

13:02.560 --> 13:03.050
Dodge!

13:10.590 --> 13:11.890
It's caught up...

13:11.890 --> 13:12.520
...to Sirknight's speed!

13:18.200 --> 13:19.710
Let's settle this right here!

13:20.280 --> 13:21.420
Use Aerial Ace!

13:30.910 --> 13:31.600
Sirknight,

13:31.870 --> 13:32.790
mega evolve!

13:49.610 --> 13:51.320
She finally mega evolved it!

13:53.880 --> 13:55.940
They've got Carne-san and Sirknight backed into a corner!

13:57.360 --> 13:59.060
Go, go, Gekkouga!

14:00.400 --> 14:02.440
Gekkouga, the real fight starts now.

14:02.770 --> 14:06.110
The stronger our opponent is, the stronger we can get too!

14:07.750 --> 14:08.770
Water Shuriken!

14:11.520 --> 14:12.080
Shadow Ball!

14:20.280 --> 14:21.400
Stronger...

14:21.620 --> 14:22.520
Aerial Ace!

14:25.090 --> 14:25.680
Reflect!

14:28.360 --> 14:28.820
That was close!

14:29.120 --> 14:30.310
They almost got it!

14:32.130 --> 14:33.730
But Gekkouga is the more aggressive of the two!

14:34.820 --> 14:36.210
Faster, faster!

14:38.350 --> 14:39.610
I have never seen these waves before.

14:40.190 --> 14:41.010
Double Team!

14:43.750 --> 14:44.330
What?

14:45.480 --> 14:46.390
What on earth...?

14:48.030 --> 14:49.690
Follow it up with Cut!

14:51.670 --> 14:52.400
Reflect!

14:58.510 --> 14:59.290
Shadow Ball!

15:00.790 --> 15:01.670
Aerial Ace!

15:05.270 --> 15:05.840
Much...

15:06.090 --> 15:07.870
Much, much stronger!

15:21.000 --> 15:21.660
Gekkouga!

15:21.920 --> 15:23.140
Water Shuriken!

15:24.640 --> 15:25.330
Shadow Ball!

15:31.440 --> 15:34.160
Go!

15:41.790 --> 15:42.440
Sirknight!

15:43.290 --> 15:45.820
Go, Gekkouga!

15:48.560 --> 15:50.110
Cut!

15:58.850 --> 15:59.440
Satoshi-kun?!

16:00.450 --> 16:01.300
Satoshi!

16:13.040 --> 16:13.700
What's going on?

16:14.160 --> 16:16.450
If <i>you</i> of all people ask us "What's going on?",

16:16.670 --> 16:18.710
It is the world's mercy that makes us answer!

16:19.180 --> 16:21.230
To prevent the world's destruction!

16:21.700 --> 16:23.870
To protect the world's peace!

16:24.330 --> 16:26.900
Carrying out the evil of love and truth,

16:27.270 --> 16:29.720
we're lovely, charmy villains!

16:30.780 --> 16:31.380
Musashi!

16:31.650 --> 16:32.260
Kojiro!

16:32.690 --> 16:35.410
For the Rocket Gang duo dashing across the galaxy,

16:35.570 --> 16:38.490
a white hole, a white tomorrow awaits us!

16:38.490 --> 16:40.190
Just kidding!

16:44.110 --> 16:45.160
The Rocket Gang!

16:45.160 --> 16:47.190
What are you doing?! We're having trouble right now!

16:47.820 --> 16:50.440
That's us; waiting for moments like this to attack!

16:50.730 --> 16:52.840
You call yourself a popular actress, don't you, Carne?

16:53.170 --> 16:56.740
Your Mega Sirknight has been taken by me, the great actress Musashi.

16:57.310 --> 17:01.920
With a mega-strengthened rope that can even hold its own against the power of a Mega Sirknight, that is!

17:02.200 --> 17:05.630
You can't cut it with just any old attack, you know...

17:07.010 --> 17:08.760
You guys take care of Satoshi-kun, please.

17:09.540 --> 17:09.880
Okay.

17:11.300 --> 17:13.280
Don't underestimate my Sirknight!

17:13.880 --> 17:14.580
Sirknight!

17:14.820 --> 17:15.750
Use your full power!

17:18.990 --> 17:20.480
Useless, useless, useless!

17:26.040 --> 17:27.230
What?!

17:27.880 --> 17:28.480
Amazing...

17:29.000 --> 17:29.960
Shadow Ball!

17:33.980 --> 17:36.030
I'll let you go for today!

17:36.240 --> 17:37.600
This feels bad!

17:46.050 --> 17:46.740
Sirknight!

17:48.880 --> 17:50.490
That really was a bit too much, wasn't it?

17:51.050 --> 17:51.510
Return.

18:02.170 --> 18:03.410
Uh... Where's Gekkouga?

18:05.560 --> 18:06.190
Are you all right?

18:07.720 --> 18:08.540
Thank goodness...

18:09.040 --> 18:10.590
Satoshi-kun, are <i>you</i> all right?

18:11.390 --> 18:11.720
Yes.

18:14.080 --> 18:14.800
Hold on to me.

18:17.070 --> 18:17.740
Thank you.

18:19.030 --> 18:20.820
I passed out again, huh?

18:23.020 --> 18:25.560
But today, I felt like we were doing fine.

18:26.310 --> 18:28.290
We were on a roll, the two us. Right?

18:37.880 --> 18:40.640
Don't forget how we did it just now, Gekkouga!

18:47.270 --> 18:49.040
At the moment, I don't know whether or not that power you and Gekkouga have...

18:49.510 --> 18:52.300
...is related to the prediction.

18:53.060 --> 18:57.740
But I'm sure you guys are capable of leading that power in the right direction.

18:58.510 --> 18:59.000
We will!

19:00.230 --> 19:01.450
I guess the next time we meet...

19:02.030 --> 19:03.660
...will be at the venue of the Kalos League?

19:04.380 --> 19:04.730
Yes!

19:05.160 --> 19:08.280
I'll make sure to get my eighth badge and participate!

19:09.080 --> 19:11.100
All right then, do your best, Satoshi-kun.

19:12.070 --> 19:13.130
Thank you very much!

19:22.860 --> 19:28.130
If Gojika-san's prediction is right and Satoshi-kun and his friends <i>are</i> involved in the Kalos crisis,

19:29.000 --> 19:31.440
there might be meaning to that power.

19:31.960 --> 19:33.950
Gekkouga, Water Shuriken!

19:37.020 --> 19:39.120
I need to investigate this further.

19:39.880 --> 19:41.750
Both to protect Satoshi-kun and his friends...

19:42.250 --> 19:42.730
...and...

19:43.250 --> 19:44.710
...to protect Kalos.

19:53.910 --> 19:55.800
I'm giving the all clear on all points.

19:57.440 --> 20:00.480
All right then, proceed with the final stage of the plan.

20:01.080 --> 20:01.400
Roger!

20:07.530 --> 20:08.640
Oh, Squishy!

20:09.040 --> 20:10.150
We're setting off!

20:11.040 --> 20:12.710
Gekkouga, let's do our best!

20:13.430 --> 20:15.180
Until we can control that power,

20:15.800 --> 20:17.370
we have to become much, much stronger!

20:19.200 --> 20:22.850
And with that, we'll win at the Eisetsu Gym and move on to the Kalos League in one go!

20:26.840 --> 20:28.370
Satoshi is on fire!

20:29.650 --> 20:30.470
Do your best!

20:31.130 --> 20:32.460
Shall we set off then?

20:33.160 --> 20:33.510
Yeah.

20:34.050 --> 20:35.740
Let's set off to the Eisetsu Gym!

20:36.590 --> 20:38.000
I'll make sure to win!

20:41.510 --> 20:45.620
Satoshi and his friends head towards the Eisestsu Gym to get the eighth badge.

20:46.440 --> 20:49.120
What kind of battle awaits them there?

20:54.760 --> 21:02.200
The winner will be
announced in mid June

20:55.400 --> 20:58.170
Today is the last day you can vote through this show.

20:58.740 --> 21:01.610
Thank you very much for participating.

21:02.200 --> 21:10.910
Airs Sunday May 8th at 8am!

21:03.160 --> 21:07.100
You can also vote via the data broadcast during this Sunday's episode of "Pokénchi".

21:07.770 --> 21:09.830
Everyone, please participate in the Elections!

21:10.410 --> 21:10.910
Finally,

21:11.080 --> 21:15.980
On sale until Friday July 15th

21:11.490 --> 21:13.240
this year's movie can be enjoyed with...

21:13.240 --> 21:15.940
...a special pre-order ticket that comes with a giveaway code for Volcanion,

21:17.060 --> 21:19.090
so everyone, please make sure to get one!

21:21.020 --> 21:26.010
Sunday May 8th at 8am!

21:21.520 --> 21:26.010
Nidoran

21:21.620 --> 21:22.730
Nidoran and Nidoking.

21:22.060 --> 21:26.010
Nidoking

21:24.190 --> 21:25.370
On Sunday at 8am!

21:28.310 --> 21:30.260
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:30.430 --> 21:31.520
Towards our next adventure!

21:32.430 --> 21:32.960
Satoshi!

21:33.450 --> 21:35.470
Can we make it a three-on-three, please?

21:35.770 --> 21:36.460
Three-on-three?

21:37.270 --> 21:42.550
I want to test how much I have grown by having another battle under the same conditions as last time!

21:42.900 --> 21:44.440
Okay, bring it on!

21:45.340 --> 21:47.790
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:48.070 --> 21:50.580
Rival Showdown! Satoshi VS Shota!!

21:50.980 --> 21:53.520
Everyone, get EXP!

21:52.470 --> 21:55.970
Next Time

21:52.470 --> 21:55.970
Rival Showdown!
Satoshi VS Shota!!

21:56.010 --> 22:06.020
Next episode:

21:56.010 --> 22:00.940
Another battle with Shota!

21:56.930 --> 22:01.520
